{"id": "1547870545662582825", "channel_id": "1545385622317965442", "author_id": "388033054129782784", "author_name": "coco_cocoa", "content": "Also just to have said it once myself despite probably sounding like an echoed sentiment, I am disappointed with the fact that there is very little variety possible in the new higher D-Tide zones and that it seems to cater to specific high Enlightenment teams and cheese strats to even make it possible. Morimens used to be one of the few outliers in the Gacha space that gave you a broad cast of fun varied characters you could play where I didn't stress too much about being able to play the characters that I simply liked or didn't feel like I had to play a char I did not want to for whatever reason. Always disappointing to see a corporate go full greedy and decide to take away the wrong thing from players, and the way BIAV has been \"responding\" to Feedback I can't attribute it to anything other but that.", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T07:24:56.130000+00:00", "thread_id": "1545385622317965442", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 7}], "thread_title": "On the D-Effect Zone Adjustments", "forum_channel_id": "1184003940082262069"}
